NAME
    gcloud alpha number-registry ipam-admin-scopes - manage IPAM admin scopes.
        This is the scope of which resources CNR can discover

SYNOPSIS
    gcloud alpha number-registry ipam-admin-scopes COMMAND
        [GCLOUD_WIDE_FLAG ...]

DESCRIPTION
    (ALPHA) Manage IPAM admin scopes. This is the scope of which resources CNR
    can discover.

GCLOUD WIDE FLAGS
    These flags are available to all commands: --help.

    Run $ gcloud help for details.

COMMANDS
    COMMAND is one of the following:

     check-availability
        (ALPHA) Check the availability of IPAM admin scopes.

     cleanup
        (ALPHA) Clean up a single IPAM admin scope resource.

     create
        (ALPHA) Create an IPAM admin scope resource.

     delete
        (ALPHA) Delete a single IPAM admin scope resource.

     describe
        (ALPHA) Gets details of a single IPAM admin scope resource.

     disable
        (ALPHA) Disable a single IPAM admin scope resource.

     list
        (ALPHA) List IPAM admin scope resources.

     update
        (ALPHA) Update the parameters of a single IPAM admin scope resource.

NOTES
    This command is currently in alpha and might change without notice. If this
    command fails with API permission errors despite specifying the correct
    project, you might be trying to access an API with an invitation-only early
    access allowlist.

